SUMMARY:60th Anniversary Gala
DESCRIPTION:  \nMay 15\, 2026\n \nBuy Tickets \nFrom protecting native plants to inspiring generations of visitors\, the Garden continues to grow because of you. Join us for an evening of celebration as we honor what we’ve accomplished and share our vision for the future: where science\, engagement\, and conservation come together with purpose and possibility. \nHonorary Chairs\nRitch & Susan Allison\nFrank & Ellen Proctor\nMike & Melissa Raley \n \n  \nGala Fundraising Focus\nHelp us enhance the Display Gardens with dynamic new outdoor educational displays and engaging signage designed to inspire\, inform\, and elevate every visitor’s experience. Your gifts will transform a walk through the Garden into a journey of discovery\, ensuring that every visitor gains a stronger connection to plants\, a deeper understanding of conservation\, and a lasting sense of purpose. \n \nAuction Items\nWeekend get-away package at Villa Pinea\nRelax in a mid-century modern home designed by architect Terry Waugh located in12-acres of forest on the edge of Chapel Hill. This four-day/three-night package includes a gift card to local restaurants\, Carolina Basketball tickets for two\, a charcuterie board\, and spirits and brew from Mother Earth Brewing. \nLive like a Parisian on the Left Bank\nEnjoy a week-long stay in a charming Paris apartment located on Rue du Cherche Midi in the heart of the 6th arrondissement.  This Paris flat includes one bedroom and two bathrooms\, with a double Murphy bed in the living room. It sleeps up to four people. Airfare not included. \nSculpture in the Garden package\nInvite your friends to join you on a small group (up to six people) studio tour and pottery demonstration by internationally-renowned Chatham County artist Mark Hewitt. This package also includes a Mark Hewitt vase\, a landscape consultation from Rachel’s Native Plants\, and a one-night stay at the Fearrington Inn among the native plant gardens of Fearrington Village. \nBirding in the Sandhills field trip \nGather 8-10 folks to follow New Hope Bird Alliance Director Tom Driscoll for an exciting and educational day trip to see and learn about the birds and natural critters who call the Sandhills home. Picnic lunch provided. \n  \n \n  \nPlanning Committee\nGail Perry\nJordan Barratt\nBetsy Bennett\nMay Bryan\nVirginia Buysse\nMelanie Christian\nEliza Cook\nHelen Frankstone\nKim Fraser\nPat Holder\nKatherine Kopp\nMia Pizzagalli\nSue Plambeck\nLiza Roberts \n \nEvent Hosts\nLongleaf\nAlice & John May\nFrank & Ellen Proctor \nMagnolia\nRitch & Susan Allison\nRufus & Linda Edmisten\nGene & Pat Holder\nKate & Jeff Hedges\nJeff Mason\nSue & Charles Plambeck\nJennifer & Al Runquist\nPhyllis Thomas & Alan Curtis\nDamon Waitt \nSassafras\nBetsy & Walter Bennett\nBecky & Munroe Cobey\nRus & Dixie Hapgood\nNicholas & Amy Penwarden\nGail Perry & Bill Cobb\nMia Pizzagalli & Ken Shelton\nMike & Melissa Raley \nDogwood\nMike & Mary Andrews\nPaula Noell & Palmer Page\nSims Preston & Olympia Stone\nKader & Margaret Ramsey\nCarol Tresolini & Tom Fiore \nFor information on becoming an Event Host see this link or contact Stephen Keith at 919-962-9458. \nBuy Tickets
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/60th-anniversary-gala/
LOCATION:The Barn at Fearrington Village\, 2000 Fearrington Village Center\, Pittsboro\, 27312\, United States
END:VEVENT
